(i) preparing and serving alcoholic and non-alcoholic beverages in accordance with LHHG's recipes and standards;

(ii) maintaining the bar area, including cleaning glassware, surfaces, and dispensing equipment;

(iii) monitoring and replenishing bar stock levels and reporting shortages to the Bar Manager or Duty Manager;

(iv) verifying the age and identification of guests purchasing alcoholic beverages in accordance with applicable law; and

(v) ensuring that all bar transactions are accurately recorded through LHHG's point-of-sale system.

2.2 PSS shall ensure that all Personnel deployed to each Site are adequately trained and competent to perform the duties described in Clause 2.1 above and that they are familiar with LHHG's standard operating procedures and code of conduct before their first Shift at any Site.

2.3 LHHG shall provide PSS with a copy of its standard operating procedures and code of conduct for each Site upon request, and PSS shall ensure that all Personnel acknowledge receipt and understanding of the same in writing.

**3. SCHEDULING PROCEDURES**

3.1 PSS shall prepare and submit a proposed staffing rota for each Site to LHHG no later than seven (7) days before the commencement of each calendar week. The rota shall:

(a) identify each Personnel by name and role;

(b) specify the Shift or Shifts to be worked by each Personnel at each Site;

(c) indicate the start and end times of each Shift; and

(d) confirm that the staffing quota for each Site is met for every Shift.

3.2 LHHG shall review each proposed rota and may request amendments to ensure that staffing levels are aligned with anticipated demand, special events, or other operational requirements. LHHG shall notify PSS of any requested amendments no later than three (3) days before the commencement of the relevant calendar week, and PSS shall incorporate such amendments into the final rota.

3.3 The final rota shall be issued by PSS no later than two (2) days before the commencement of the relevant calendar week and shall be binding on both Parties, subject to Clause 3.4 and Clause 4 below.

4.2 The rates set out in the Rate Card are inclusive of all statutory deductions, contributions, and levies required by law, including but not limited to the Nigerian Social Insurance Trust Fund (NSITF) contributions, the National Housing Fund (NHF) contributions, and the Industrial Training Fund (ITF) contributions, where applicable. PSS shall be solely responsible for the remittance of all such deductions and contributions to the relevant authorities and shall indemnify and hold harmless LHHG from and against any claim, penalty, fine, or liability arising from any failure by PSS to make such remittances on time or at all. For the avoidance of doubt, the rates set out in the Rate Card do not include Value Added Tax (VAT), which shall be added to all invoices at the prevailing rate as required by the Federal Inland Revenue Service (FIRS).

4.3 The rates set out in the Rate Card are net of any agency or recruitment fees, and no additional charges, surcharges, or fees of any nature shall be payable by LHHG except as expressly provided in this Agreement or as may be agreed in writing by the Parties from time to time. Without limiting the generality of the foregoing, PSS shall bear all costs associated with the recruitment, training, uniforming, and transportation of Personnel to and from the Sites, and no such costs shall be passed on to LHHG.

4.4 The rates set out in the Rate Card may be reviewed annually by the Parties, with effect from the anniversary of the Commencement Date. Any such review shall be conducted in good faith, and any adjustment to the rates shall be agreed in writing by the Parties no later than thirty (30) days before the effective date of the adjustment. In the event that the Parties fail to agree on any adjustment to the rates within the said thirty (30) day period, the existing rates shall continue to apply until such time as an agreement is reached. PSS shall not be entitled to withhold the provision of Services or to reduce the quality or quantity of Services in any way pending the outcome of any rate review.

4.5 PSS shall submit to LHHG a detailed invoice on a bi-weekly basis, no later than five (5) business days after the end of the relevant bi-weekly period. Each invoice shall be in a form reasonably acceptable to LHHG and shall include, without limitation:

(a) the name and role of each Personnel deployed during the relevant bi-weekly period;

(b) the Site at which each Personnel worked;

(c) the date and the start and end times of each Shift worked by each Personnel;

