(d) the number of hours worked by each Personnel, broken down by Shift;

(e) the applicable hourly rate for each Personnel in accordance with the Rate Card;

(f) the total amount payable for each Personnel;

(g) a summary of any overtime hours worked, where such overtime has been authorised in accordance with Clause 4.6;

(h) a summary of any deductions or adjustments, including deductions for unauthorised absences or late arrivals, in accordance with Clause 5.5; and

(i) the total amount due for the bi-weekly period, exclusive and inclusive of VAT.

4.6 Overtime shall only be payable where it has been authorised in advance in writing by an authorised representative of LHHG. Authorisation may be given on a per-Shift basis or for a defined period, and shall specify the maximum number of overtime hours authorised. Overtime hours shall be compensated at the rate of one and one-half (1.5) times the applicable hourly rate set out in the Rate Card. PSS shall not include any overtime hours in an invoice unless such hours have been authorised in accordance with this Clause 4.6 and are supported by time records that comply with Clause 5.3.

**CLAUSE 7 — CONFIDENTIALITY**

7.1 Each Party shall treat as confidential and shall not, without the prior written consent of the other Party, disclose to any third party any Confidential Information of the other Party, save that:

(a) either Party may disclose Confidential Information to its officers, employees, professional advisers, insurers and subcontractors to the extent necessary for the performance of its obligations or the exercise of its rights under this Agreement, provided that such persons are bound by obligations of confidentiality no less onerous than those set out in this Clause 7;

(b) either Party may disclose Confidential Information to the extent required by law, by any court of competent jurisdiction, by any regulatory authority, or by the rules of any recognised stock exchange;

(c) either Party may disclose Confidential Information to the extent that such information has entered the public domain otherwise than through a breach of this Clause 7;

(d) either Party may disclose Confidential Information to its auditors, tax advisers and legal counsel; and

(e) PSS may use aggregated, anonymised data derived from the provision of the Services for its own internal analytical and benchmarking purposes, provided that such use does not reveal, directly or indirectly, the identity of LHHG or any of its customers, guests or Personnel.

7.2 For the purposes of this Agreement, "Confidential Information" means all information (whether oral, written, or in electronic or other form) disclosed by or on behalf of one Party to the other Party in connection with this Agreement, including without limitation:

(a) the terms of this Agreement, including the Rates and the Rate Card;

(b) any information relating to the business, affairs, customers, clients, suppliers, plans, financial position, operations, or personnel of the disclosing Party;

(c) any information relating to the Sites, including security arrangements, access protocols, and operational procedures;

(d) any personal data of Personnel or of LHHG's employees, customers, or guests;

(e) any information marked as confidential at the time of disclosure; and

(f) any information which, from the circumstances of disclosure, a reasonable person would understand to be confidential.

7.3 The obligations of confidentiality set out in this Clause 7 shall not apply to information which the receiving Party can demonstrate by written records:

(a) was lawfully in its possession prior to the date of disclosure;

(b) was independently developed by the receiving Party without reference to the disclosing Party's Confidential Information;

(c) was lawfully received from a third party who was not under an obligation of confidentiality to the disclosing Party; or

(d) is required to be disclosed to a third party in order for the receiving Party to perform its obligations under this Agreement, but only to the extent of such required disclosure.

7.4 Each Party shall:

(a) use Confidential Information of the other Party only for the purposes of performing its obligations or exercising its rights under this Agreement;

(b) take reasonable steps to protect the Confidential Information of the other Party from unauthorised disclosure or use, and in any event no less stringent steps than it takes to protect its own confidential information of a similar nature; and

(c) notify the other Party promptly upon becoming aware of any actual or suspected unauthorised disclosure or use of Confidential Information.

7.5 The provisions of this Clause 7 shall survive the expiry or termination of this Agreement for a period of five (5) years, provided that in respect of any Confidential Information which constitutes personal data, the provisions of this Clause 7 shall continue to apply for so long as such personal data remains in the possession or control of the receiving Party, subject to applicable data protection law.

"Agreement" means this Food Supply Agreement together with all Schedules attached hereto, as amended from time to time in writing by the Parties;

"Business Day" means any day other than a Saturday, Sunday, or public holiday in Nigeria;

"Confirmation of Order" means the written acknowledgement of an Order issued by FCFD in accordance with Clause 5;

"Contract Price" means the price payable by LHHG for Products as set out in the applicable Price List;

"Delivery Location" means the loading bay or designated receiving point at the relevant LHHG premises as specified in the Order;

"Force Majeure" means an event or circumstance beyond the reasonable control of the affected Party, including but not limited to acts of God, war, terrorism, riot, fire, flood, storm, earthquake, epidemic, pandemic, strike, lockout, government action or regulation, or failure of public utilities or transportation networks;

"Order" means a purchase order issued by LHHG to FCFD in accordance with Clause 5;

"Party" and "Parties" shall have the meaning assigned in the opening paragraph;

"Price List" means the schedule of prices for Products as published by FCFD to LHHG from time to time in accordance with Clause 8;

"Products" means the food products, supplies, and consumables listed in Schedule 1, together with any additional products agreed in writing by the Parties;

"Quality Specification" means the quality standards, grades, and specifications applicable to the Products as set out in Schedule 2;

"Service Levels" means the service levels set out in Schedule 3.

