1.3 Clause headings are inserted for convenience only and shall not affect the interpretation of this Agreement.

1.4 References to Clauses and Schedules are, unless otherwise stated, references to clauses of and schedules to this Agreement.

**2. TERM AND COMMENCEMENT**

2.1 This Agreement shall commence on 20 May 2024 and shall continue in force for an initial period of twelve (12) months, expiring on 19 May 2025 (the "Initial Term").

2.2 Upon expiry of the Initial Term, this Agreement shall automatically renew for successive periods of twelve (12) months (each a "Renewal Term") unless either Party gives the other not less than sixty (60) days' written notice of its intention not to renew, such notice to expire at the end of the then-current Term.

2.3 The Initial Term and any Renewal Term are together referred to as the "Term".

**3. SUPPLY OF PRODUCTS**

3.1 FCFD shall supply, and LHHG shall purchase, the Products in accordance with the terms of this Agreement.

3.2 FCFD shall use its reasonable endeavours to supply Products that meet the Quality Specification set out in Schedule 2. LHHG shall be entitled to reject any Products that fail to meet the Quality Specification, subject to prompt notification and return of such Products in accordance with Clause 9.

3.3 FCFD shall ensure that all Products supplied under this Agreement comply with all applicable laws, regulations, and standards in force in Nigeria, including but not limited to the National Agency for Food and Drug Administration and Control (NAFDAC) requirements, the Standards Organisation of Nigeria (SON) requirements, and any applicable Islamic dietary requirements where specified in the Order.

3.4 FCFD shall maintain appropriate food safety management systems, including HACCP-based controls, and shall provide LHHG with reasonable evidence of such systems upon request.

